18, 85&#x2013;95. 10.1093/emboj/18.1.85</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1093/emboj/18.1.85</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC1171105</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">9878053</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Tresse E., Salomons F. A., Vesa J., Bott L. C., Kimonis V., Yao T. P., et al. (2010). VCP/p97 is essential for maturation of ubiquitin-containing autophagosomes and this function is impaired by mutations that cause IBMPFD. Autophagy 6, 217&#x2013;227. 10.4161/auto.6.2.11014</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.4161/auto.6.2.11014</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC2929010</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">20104022</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Vabulas R. M., Raychaudhuri S., Hayer-Hartl M., Hartl F. U. (2010). Protein folding in the cytoplasm and the heat shock response. Cold Spring Harb. Perspect. Biol. 2:a004390. 10.1101/cshperspect.a004390</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1101/cshperspect.a004390</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC2982175</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">21123396</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Valastyan J. S., Lindquist S. (2014). Mechanisms of protein-folding diseases at a glance. Dis. Model. Mech. 7, 9&#x2013;14. 10.1242/dmm.013474</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1242/dmm.013474</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC3882043</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">24396149</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Wang Q., Li L., Ye Y. (2008). Inhibition of p97-dependent protein degradation by Eeyarestatin I. J. Biol. Chem. 283, 7445&#x2013;7454. 10.1074/jbc.M708347200</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1074/jbc.M708347200</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC2276333</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">18199748</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Wang Q., Shinkre B. A., Lee J. G., Weniger M. A., Liu Y.,